Subject: [PATCH 10/18] feat: plugin hooks for full-page routes and sidebar links
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 2.1 (2026-10-12)  2.0 = merged set of 11 patches; 2.1 = Hook.PageLink (link on Settings > License)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0009)

(was 0016 v1.0)
- Client plugins can register a full-page route (Hook.Route) and a link in
  the main sidebar menu (Hook.SidebarLink), each with an enabled(team, user)
  check.
- Hook.PageLink (2.1): a plugin adds a link to a core page; page "license"
  shows it as a row with an "Open" button in Settings > License (used by the
  license management plugin instead of a sidebar link and a settings item).
- Nothing visible changes without a plugin that uses them (kms-subscribers,
  ssozia-users). Their install scripts check for SidebarLink in
  PluginManager.ts, so the new number does not matter to them.

Files (4; N = new, M = modified, D = deleted):
  M app/components/Sidebar/App.tsx
  M app/routes/authenticated.tsx
  M app/scenes/Settings/License.tsx
  M app/utils/PluginManager.ts

---
---

